# 4ndr0666 Hyprland User Configuration

This directory contains user-owned Lua configuration and overrides loaded by `config/hypr/hyprland.lua`.

1. Do not rename files that are loaded by `hyprland.lua` unless you also update the corresponding `require()` path.

2. `UserConfigs` and `UserScripts` are user-owned and are preserved by repository upgrades.

3. Hyprland breaking changes may require updates to the user-owned Lua modules. Use the current Hyprland 0.56+ documentation when changing configuration schema.

4. Keep machine-specific defaults, keybinds, settings, animations, window rules, and workspace rules in their designated user modules rather than modifying vendor defaults unnecessarily.

5. When a default configuration needs correction, prefer fixing the canonical default module and keeping machine-specific behavior in the appropriate `UserConfigs` override.